A few days ago, in the &quot;Arena Champions&quot; thread (https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/challenge-arena-champions-8877), Nepycros posted the following strategy that he (she?) used to accumulate ridiculous amounts of Favor against Kaargra Warfang, with a team of (in order) Grandpa Legacy, Dark Visionary, Argent Adept, and Wraith: &nbsp;

&nbsp;


[quote="Nepycros"]


Perfect lockdown. Take Down happens to be an Ongoing, which Mental Divergence can infinitely recycle. Not only that, but Argent Adept helps Legacy to draw AND play Take Down out of turn. Legacy becomes immune to Melee damage, Wraith reduces all the damage the environment deals to 0, and then picks them off with some heavy damage powers. So the Villain cannot play cards or deal damage, and the environment cannot deal damage.&nbsp;

[/quote]

&nbsp;

I experimented with the technique against Kaargra, and without even trying very hard, won 54-7. &nbsp;It then struck me that this technique could be nigh-unbeatable (absent really bad card draws) against just about any villain. &nbsp;I tried it against Advanced Progeny (one of my bete-noirs from another thread), and neutered him in two rounds. &nbsp;Granted, I had some really good draws, but once you get the loop going in which the villain can&#39;t draw or deal damage (thanks to a profusion of Stun Bolts), the environment damage is neutered, and Dark Visionary is getting rid of any problematic environment cards that could kill your strategy, I&#39;m not sure any villain can get out of it. &nbsp;I&#39;m thinking about trying it next against Advanced Chairman in Rook City. &nbsp;If I can kill him there with no trouble, this might be the unbeatable team/loop. &nbsp; Thoughts?

&nbsp;

[quote="Powerhound_2000"]

Also keep in mind that Take Down doesn&#39;t prevent the Operative from putting Underbosses into play so even if you had gotten that you&#39;d still have to deal with them for a bit. &nbsp; &nbsp;

[/quote]

Yeah, I was counting on enough DR from Legacy to offset the damage from the underbosses and thugs to stave things off until I got the combo going. &nbsp;I just never got the combo going. &nbsp;

[quote="Powerhound_2000"]

Brain Burn does not help with the Operative pulling out Underbosses. &nbsp; Brain Burn only helps with the Thugs. &nbsp;

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Yeah, but if you can Brain Burn the Thugs, then pulling out Underbosses isn&#39;t that big of a deal. &nbsp;The only two Underbosses that can do anything without Thugs to pull out of the trash are Contract and Muscle. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

On my fourth try, I got lucky and Brain Burned Chairman on the first round. &nbsp;After that, it took a little while to get the Take Down/Mental Divergence combo out, but there wasn&#39;t much Chairman could do to hurt me in the meantime. &nbsp;Once the combo was out, I killed the Underbosses, then Chairman and Operative, at my leisure. &nbsp;It took a little while because Wraith was the only one really doing damage, but once the combo was out, it was simply a matter of time and patience; there was nothing Chairman or the environment could really do to prevent it at that point. &nbsp;
